   "U028": "Scoring breaks and multiple casinos",
   "U029": "### Scoring breaks and multiple casinos\n\nRecord casino points by moving your chip on the **printed scoring track**. Numeric gaps are **breaks**: you must earn enough **from that individual casino** to reach the next printed value. Stop before a break you cannot cross and lose unusable excess points; do not save them for later.\n\nFor example, from **8**: an award of **1** leaves you on 8; **2 or 3** takes you to **10**; **4 or 5** takes you to **12**.\n\nWhen several casinos pay you points on one turn, score them **individually, from smallest to largest**, choosing the order of equal-size casinos. You cannot combine their awards to cross a break. Several separate one-tile casinos therefore still cannot move a chip from 8 to 10.",
